  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated and sustainable rural development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The diocesan Caritas organisation for Baucau used a participatory process to design this project with the full involvement of the beneficiaries.  It aims to empower and raise the living standards of a very poor rural community by improving food security at the household level through support to rice production and horticulture (vegetable growing), developing income-generation opportunities for women and vulnerable people through weaving of tais (traditional Timorese cloth), community reforestation,   Inputs include group animation and building up of local leadership, initial start-up capital (funding, tools, seeds), training in practical production skills and bookkeeping, and marketing studies.  The community is being encouraged to set up a tree nursery, and to achieve seed sovereignty through saving and sharing seeds.  The reforestation component, together with training on soil conservation and water management, are expected gradually to mitigate local environmental challenges including the new challenges arising from climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
